{"title":"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Intuition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Intuition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, evaluate the sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab23b66f352367a017f0e97492955f7eababefb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] = \\Big[\\frac{n + 1}{2}\\Big] + \\Big[\\frac{n + 2}{4}\\Big] + \\cdots + \\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] + \\cdots\\]\" width=\"454\" height=\"48\" />\n(The symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I shall prove that the summation is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Let the binary representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c94fec2f57a86b0b92d1453c45903ad01ab86e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{d_xd_{x-1}\\dots d_1d_0}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a2d8f08b9b80901a36a4021ab10dd7f0edffe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i\\in\\{0,1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7cef981d867655a8b247d733c7d12ff28573267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\lfloor \\log_2 n\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" />. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd0c0b79232351182831e654c2e90c4050feb50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54c79579e91033ae383f8ab1688f5b81e6f7479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Big[\\frac{n + 2^i}{2^{i+1}}\\Big]=\\Big[\\frac{n}{2^{i+1}}\\Big]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"141\" height=\"39\" />; and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f82e628878a08dc28684b279055f1615eb91563c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f55ccd236836945c103f4958b32f778d4e9b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Big[\\frac{n + 2^i}{2^{i+1}}\\Big]=\\Big[\\frac{n}{2^{i+1}}\\Big]+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"39\" />. Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a0a7529cb79963255068cb5dd57656bd39e289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Big[\\frac{n + 2^i}{2^{i+1}}\\Big]=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"39\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0faed124ce03e0a1d17d4a4f62d656030dda980b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\geq x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore the given sum is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a48638a8a228b14ef9f8a0cc35cf391a85dffd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] =S+\\sum_{k=0}^{x} \\bigg[\\frac{n}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg]\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of 1's in the binary representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula\" title=\"Legendre&#39;s Formula\">Legendre's Formula</a> states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/4420e9dcc4e2106cbfe3994d903e9c89fb37c1a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-S=\\sum_{k=0}^{x} \\bigg[\\frac{n}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"150\" height=\"48\" />, which proves the assertion. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/becdcf89a9cd0b8e1709555685192daef4d32b61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 2^k \\text{mod }2^{k+1} \\longrightarrow \\left[\\frac{n+1+2^k}{2^{k+1}}\\right] - \\left[\\frac{n+2^k}{2^{k+1}}\\right] = 1 \\text{ and } \\left[\\frac{n+1+2^k}{2^{k+1}}\\right] - \\left[\\frac{n+2^k}{2^{k+1}}\\right] = 0 \\text{ otherwise.}\\]\" width=\"731\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d1687a5cf370d600e9e3bc7f27ccad8e581345.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D = [d \\text{ } | \\text{ } \\exists \\text{ } s \\in \\mathbb{N} \\text{ such that } d \\equiv 2^{s-1} \\text{ mod } 2^s] = \\mathbb{N} \\longrightarrow \\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n+1 + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] - \\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] = 1,\\]\" width=\"702\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>so the result is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ilovepi3.14\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Hermite's identity, for real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e011d6ce23412dd56c813be05be36ccc07ab0ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigg[ x + \\frac12 \\bigg] = \\bigg[ 2x \\bigg] - \\bigg[ x \\bigg].\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Hence our sum telescopes: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f55916cbcd3255840d45965a606b86a4e1bd42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n + 2^k}{2^{k + 1}}\\bigg] = \\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty\\bigg[\\frac{n}{2^{k + 1}} + \\frac12 \\bigg] = \\sum_{k = 0}^\\infty \\left( \\bigg[\\frac{n}{2^{k}} \\bigg] - \\bigg[ \\frac{n}{2^{k+1}} \\bigg] \\right) = \\bigg[ n \\bigg].\\]\" width=\"502\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Maximilian113\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Intuition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Intuition)\">Solution 4 (Intuition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Intuition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The key observation is to interpret each term as counting integers.\n</p><p>The first term\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebde1329a7419e96e7033a661197cc0015ccc7c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big[\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Big]\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />\ncounts the odd integers up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>The second term\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8ae16661f7cbdafd3b0d029ab8a46a1284c9ac3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big[\\frac{n+2}{4}\\Big]\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />\ncounts the integers divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The third term\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d42d0e46756d5e9ebefa22996d81099f7c0fcec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big[\\frac{n+4}{8}\\Big]\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />\ncounts the integers divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In general,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfaec771e57faf2824cce040dc75046d470f2cad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big[\\frac{n+2^k}{2^{k+1}}\\Big]\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"39\" />\ncounts the integers up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> but not by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473b67382183fc823e117858fef19aaf2ec23948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>But every positive integer has a unique highest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dividing it. Thus every integer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> appears in exactly one of these groups.\n</p><p>Therefore the sum of the sizes of all these groups is simply\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc513de5a31b43c4965457f33247ae4739b629b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{n}.\\]\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO\" title=\"1968 IMO\">1968 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=215131&amp;sid=6798c42a2ab57f3ca82ffba974ed589c#p215131\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016184803\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 262/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 865/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 50/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8787/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.549      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.549      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10882:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016184803 and revision id 290167. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}